{"run_id": "planned-4207-s04-51fb5d", "t": 5.95, "type": "model_call", "step": 4, "purpose": "execute", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "latency_s": 1.164, "usage": {"input_tokens": 3002, "output_tokens": 200, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "prompt_tokens": 3002}, "cost_usd": 0.0014006, "tool_calls": [{"name": "pulls_open", "input": {"title": "Fix weekly scheduled export skipping the first week when created on the same day", "branch": "repomind/issue-4207", "body": "File: src/export/scheduler.ts\n\nIn `nextRunAt`, the weekly case unconditionally advances by 7 days without checking whether `next <= from`, unlike the daily case. When a weekly schedule is created before the run hour on the same day, `next` is already in the future relative to `from`, but adding 7 days skips the current week's run. Fix this by adding the same `if (next <= from) next.setUTCDate(next.getUTCDate() + 7);` logic (or advancing by 7 days only when `next <= from`) so a newly created schedule runs on its starting day if created before the scheduled hour.", "issue": "issue-4207"}}], "tools": ["pulls_open"], "request": null, "text": ""}
